Third-party model attribution
=============================

The example 3D robot and positioner models bundled under
`frontend/public/models/` are derived from the ROS-Industrial "motoman"
repository:

  https://github.com/ros-industrial/motoman
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Specifically:
  * frontend/public/models/ar2010/        <- motoman_ar2010_support
  * frontend/public/models/motopos_d500/  <- motoman_motopos_d500_support

The URDF files were generated from the packages' xacro sources using
tools/xacro_to_urdf.py; the STL meshes are unmodified copies of the
packages' visual *and* collision meshes (collision hulls are not rendered).
A copy of the Apache-2.0 license is available at:

  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

These CAD/mesh models are provided by ROS-Industrial for simulation and
visualisation. They are approximate representations; for certified geometry and
kinematics use the official Yaskawa CAD / MotoSim models (see docs/MODELS.md).
